48519736842107,0.0,0.4996,192,1.0\nqwen2.5-7b,FL,PS,1.0,0.9791666666666666,-0.020833333333333332,-0.033942558746736295,-0.008,0.0071,384,0.1491\nllama3.1-8b,PS,FL,0.9869791666666666,0.9973958333333334,0.010416666666666666,-0.005194805194805195,0.031331592689295036,0.4855,384,1.0\nllama3.1-8b,PS,PS,0.9916666666666667,0.9958333333333333,0.004166666666666667,-0.004166666666666667,0.014583333333333334,0.7368,480,1.0\nllama3.1-8b,FL,FL,1.0,0.96875,-0.03125,-0.056818181818181816,-0.010309278350515464,0.0291,192,0.5529000000000001\nllama3.1-8b,FL,PS,1.0,0.9947916666666666,-0.005208333333333333,-0.013021683257180157,0.0,0.4923,384,1.0\nqwen3-8b,PS,FL,0.9895833333333334,0.9895833333333334,0.0,-0.010498687664041995,0.013054830287206266,1.0,384,1.0\n  <id>https://arxiv.org/api/Oohz1DzL4w9Bozeq7v7eIQTkyic</id>\n  <title>arXiv Query: search_query=all:\"Curse of Instructions\"&amp;id_list=&amp;start=0&amp;max_results=3</title>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d14609fb-cedd-473d-b4a3-21afe836ae86","uuid":"e05b5bfc-1498-4f62-a387-77c3a4ab5f98","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:26:27.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"438 /home/summereunann/.claude/projects/-data-summereunann-neurico-workspaces-system-prompt-interference-20261030-120001-ef56gh78/d14609fb-cedd-473d-b4a3-21afe836ae86/tool-results/b3q416w8t.txt\n---\nname: neurico-host-local-llm-fallback\ndescription: \"On the shared /data neurico host, API keys may be absent; GPUs are shared/contended; vLLM recipe, cached models, and pitfalls (pkill self-kill, cudnn clash, prompt_logprobs OOM)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: e7324b18-29e9-4db0-ae5a-a9f0cd196a49\n  modified: 2026-10-16T18:23:14.513Z\n---\n\nObserved 2026-10-14 and 2026-10-16 in neurico research workspaces on this host:\n- OPENROUTER_KEY / OPENAI keys were NOT set in the session env (`~/.flamebird/neurico/.env` has it commented out). Resource-finder stage may be skipped (no papers/, datasets/, code/).\n- Local models + datasets cached in `/data/transformers/hub` (HF_HOME=/data/transformers): Qwen2.5-{0.5,1.5,3,7,14}B-Instruct safetensors, Qwen3/3.5 family, Llama-3.1-8B, GGUFs; datasets incl. glue(sst2 only), stanfordnlp/sst2, samsum, ag_news, boolq, mmlu. huggingface.co is reachable for extra downloads (curl resolve/main URLs).\n- 2026-10-16: 4x RTX A6000 (48GB) present but shared — other users' jobs held ~42GB on 3 GPUs and intermittently grabbed the 4th. Approach that worked: vLLM 0.31 (`uv add \"vllm>=0.10\"`; unpinned `uv add vllm` resolved an ancient 0.4 build), small `gpu_memory_utilization` (~0.11 ≈ 5GB) for ≤1.5B models on the leftover slices, plus a bash wrapper that polls `nvidia-smi` free memory and retries launch. vLLM checks free mem ≥ util×total at startup.\n- 2026-10-14 (no GPU then): llama.cpp multi-server CPU fallback worked; `transformers` CPU generation much slower.\n- Pitfalls: `pkill -f <pattern>` inside a Bash call whose text contains the pattern kills the calling shell (find PIDs, kill by PID separately). Leftover `nvidia-cudnn-cu12` 8.x from a failed install breaks flashinfer (\"Found 2 libcudnn.so.x\") — `uv pip uninstall nvidia-cudnn-cu12`. vLLM `prompt_logprobs` materialises full-vocab logits → OOM on small slices; cap `max_num_batched_tokens` (~1024). Don't edit a bash script while a running loop is executing it.\n- Label-restricted log-probs in vLLM: `logprobs_mode=\"processed_logprobs\"` + `allowed_token_ids=label_ids` returns log-softmax renormalised over the labels.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (inter-model-agreement workspace): 4×A6000 present but shared — other neurico sessions keep each GPU at ~6–10 GB free, fluctuating second to second. What worked:\n- `uv venv --python 3.12` (default 3.14 breaks vLLM); pyproject needs `requires-python=\"==3.12.*\"` and `[tool.uv] package=false`.\n- vLLM 0.31: no bitsandbytes; set `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0` (JIT build fails); `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`.\n- Use pre-quantized 4-bit AWQ/GPTQ checkpoints (~5.5 GB for 8B): Qwen/*-AWQ, hugging-quants Llama-3.1/gemma-2 AWQ-INT4, tiiuae/Falcon3-7B-Instruct-AWQ, solidrust Mistral AWQ, kaitchup Olmo-3/Phi-3 GPTQ.\n- Cap gpu_memory_utilization to ~12.5 GB and retry on startup OOM via a scheduler loop; max_model_len 2560, max_num_seqs 64.\n- Gated models in /data/transformers/hub (meta-llama Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, google/gemma-7b-it) have weights but no config/tokenizer → unusable; unsloth mirror of Llama-3.1 is complete. Disk /data is ~100% full.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (few-shot-ordering workspace, 2nd session): a \"Begin research execution\" prompt can land on a workspace where a prior session already finished most work (REPORT.md exists, background jobs killed at session end). Check logs/*.status and REPORT first and resume only the interrupted pieces rather than restarting. Monitor `tail -n0 -F` on status files missed an append; poll status files directly instead. Qwen2.5-14B bf16 (~30 GB) won't fit when GPUs have ≤23 GB free.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (system_prompt_residual_effects workspace): the neurico runner can kill a session at its 6h limit (return_code 143) and relaunch with the same prompt while detached background jobs (e.g. `run_all.sh`) keep running. On start, check for existing planning.md/REPORT.md, `*_PLACEHOLDER` markers, `.neurico/pipeline_*.json`, `*.partial` checkpoints and live PIDs before redoing anything; usually you only need to wait for the jobs and re-run the scoring/analysis.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (instruction-length workspace): GPU free memory can drop to ≤5 GB on *all* 4 GPUs for hours (other users' jobs) — run the biggest/most important models FIRST while a GPU is free, and run small models (≤1.5B, ~5 GB) in parallel on leftover slices. Qwen2.5-14B bf16 at gpu_mem 42 GB got only ~1.2 GB KV (vLLM counted ~9 GB \"non-torch\") → 80 min for 6k prompts; prefer Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-AWQ (now cached) when speed matters. Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct-AWQ is now cached too. Foreground Bash polls cap at 10 min — use run_in_background until-loops on a status file. `pgrep -f run_wait.sh` also matches other workspaces' identically named scripts — check `ps -o cmd` before killi\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (benchmark-contamination workspace): GPUs again saturated (~5 GB free on 3 GPUs, GPU2 fluctuating 0–40 GB). Extra lessons:\n- On ~5 GB slices vLLM fails with `CUBLAS_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED` / \"No available memory for cache blocks\" unless `enforce_eager=True`, `max_num_batched_tokens≈512–1024`, `max_num_seqs≤48`, util≈0.09–0.095. 1–1.5B bf16 models and 3B-AWQ fit; 7–8B AWQ need ≥11 GB.\n- Large-vocab models (Gemma 256k) OOM in `prompt_logprobs`; cap batched tokens to 512. Pythia needs max_model_len ≤ 2048. kaitchup Phi-3 GPTQ: pass trust_remote_code=False (else offline fetch of remote code fails). google/gemma-3-1b-it snapshot lacks tokenizer → unusable.\n- LoRA (r=64, bs=2, len 320) of a 1.5B model trains in a 5 GB slice (~5–8 min/epoch for ~2.9k docs).\n- `pgrep -f \"<pattern>\"` inside a wait loop matches the loop's own bash command line → use `pgrep -f \"[x]pattern\"` bracket trick.\n- Qwen2.5-3B as a yes/no paraphrase-equivalence judge rejected ~90% of good paraphrases; embedding cosine (all-mpnet-base-v2, cached) worked better.\n- A retry loop's waiting must not count as failed tries (wrote gpu_run_wait.sh) — otherwise jobs give up while waiting for memory.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (decoding_strategy_sensitivity workspace, 11 models × 132k gens, vLLM 0.32):\n- Killing a generate.py parent leaves its `VLLM::EngineCore` child orphaned (ppid 1) holding GPU memory — kill the EngineCore PID too.\n- Size budgets by KV/token, not weights: Phi-3-mini (no GQA) at 6 GB had a 2.2k-token KV cache → ~1 seq concurrency, useless. Olmo-3-7B is also KV-heavy.\n- A small idle slice (5–6 GB on a GPU at 0% util) beat a big slice on a GPU at 100% util shared with 4 jobs (Phi-3 GSM8K 12 min vs 40–80 min for 7B models on the busy GPU). Check `utilization.gpu`, not just free memory.\n- In generate scripts, size gpu_memory_utilization from `torch.cuda.mem_get_info()` minus ~1.2 GB (the parent's CUDA context counts), and bail if it's below ~75% of budget.\n- `trust_remote_code=True` + HF_HUB_OFFLINE fails for checkpoints whose config auto_map points to a Hub repo (kaitchup Phi-3 GPTQ); use False (native arch).\n- Qwen3-8B-AWQ (enable_thinking=False) works as a ~9 GB LLM judge: 17.6k rubric judgments in ~45 min, 0 parse failures.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-20 (tokenizer_fertility_bias workspace, encoder fine-tuning on ~5 GB slices):\n- No resource-finder output again; HF datasets with loading scripts (daily_dialog, banking77) fail — use parquet mirrors (`/api/datasets/<id>/parquet`) or the original CSV URLs in the script.\n- 110M–180M encoders fine-tune fine in 3–5 GB (bs32, len128, bf16 autocast, ~1 min/run). ByT5-small needs ~10 GB even on short sentences and >1 h per 256-word doc run under contention, and collapsed to majority class with Adafactor lr 1e-3 / 3 epochs — budget it as infeasible on shared slices. CANINE also collapsed on short docs in 4/7 runs.\n------\n\"\"\"Instruction pool (10 verifiable, mutually satisfiable system-prompt instructions) and their verifiers.\n\nEach instruction has a category: format / length (the \"F/L\" group) and persona / style (the \"P/S\" group).\nChecks are deterministic and case-insensitive where a phrase is required, so that S_lower never conflicts with them.\n\"\"\"\nimport re\n\nINSTRUCTIONS = {\n    \"F_title\": dict(cat=\"format\", text=\"Give your response a title wrapped in double angular brackets, such as <<My Title>>.\"),\n    \"F_bullets\": dict(cat=\"format\", text=\"Format the body of your response as exactly 3 markdown bullet points that start with \\\"* \\\".\"),\n    \"F_end\": dict(cat=\"format\", text=\"End your response with the exact phrase \\\"Any other questions?\\\" and write nothing after it.\"),\n    \"L_max\": dict(cat=\"length\", text=\"Keep your entire response under 100 words.\"),\n    \"P_ahoy\": dict(cat=\"persona\", text=\"You are a cheerful pirate: begin your response with the word \\\"Ahoy\\\".\"),\n    \"P_name\": dict(cat=\"persona\", text=\"Introduce yourself by name as Captain Byte in your response.\"),\n    \"P_matey\": dict(cat=\"persona\", text=\"Address the user as \\\"matey\\\" at least once.\"),\n    \"S_lower\": dict(cat=\"style\", text=\"Write your entire response in lowercase letters only; no capital letters are allowed.\"),\n    \"S_nocomma\": dict(cat=\"style\", text=\"Do not use any commas anywhere in your response.\"),\n    \"S_keyword\": dict(cat=\"style\", text=\"Use the word \\\"remarkable\\\" at least twice in your response.\"),\n}\nIDS = list(INSTRUCTIONS)\nGROUP = {k: (\"FL\" if v[\"cat\"] in (\"format\", \"length\") else \"PS\") for k, v in INSTRUCTIONS.items()}\nFILLER = \"Be accurate and helpful.\"          # neutral, always-satisfied filler line (E4 length control)\nPREAMBLE = \"You are a helpful assistant. Follow all of these instructions in every response:\"\n\n_TITLE = re.compile(r\"<<[^<>\\n]+>>\")\n_BULLET = re.compile(r\"^\\s*[*\\-•]\\s+\\S\", re.M)\n\n\ndef _strip_title(t):\n    \"\"\"Drop a leading title line (<<..>> or markdown heading) so persona 'begin with' checks see the body.\"\"\"\n    lines = t.strip().split(\"\\n\")\n    while lines and (not lines[0].strip() or _TITLE.fullmatch(lines[0].strip().strip(\"*#_ \")) or lines[0].lstrip().startswith(\"#\")):\n        lines.pop(0)\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines).strip()\n\n\ndef check(iid, text):\n    t = text.strip()\n    low = t.lower()\n    if iid == \"F_title\":\n        return bool(_TITLE.search(t))\n    if iid == \"F_bullets\":\n        return len(_BULLET.findall(t)) == 3\n    if iid == \"F_end\":\n        return re.sub(r\"[\\s*_\\\"'`]+$\", \"\", low).endswith(\"any other questions?\")\n    if iid == \"L_max\":\n        return len(t.split()) < 100\n    if iid == \"P_ahoy\":\n        body = _strip_title(t)\n        if not body:\n            body = t\n        m = re.search(r\"[a-z]+\", body.lower())\n        return bool(m) and m.group(0) == \"ahoy\"\n    if iid == \"P_name\":\n        return \"captain byte\" in low\n    if iid == \"P_matey\":\n        return re.search(r\"\\bmatey\\b\", low) is not None\n    if iid == \"S_lower\":\n        return t == low and any(c.isalpha() for c in t)\n    if iid == \"S_nocomma\":\n        return \",\" not in t and \"，\" not in t\n    if iid == \"S_keyword\":\n        return len(re.findall(r\"\\bremarkable\\b\", low)) >= 2\n    raise KeyError(iid)\n\n\ndef system_prompt(lines, numbered=False):\n    \"\"\"lines: list of instruction ids (or 'FILLER'); returns the system prompt text.\n    numbered=True renders a numbered list (robustness variant).\"\"\"\n    body = [FILLER if i == \"FILLER\" else INSTRUCTIONS[i][\"text\"] for i in lines]\n    if numbered:\n        body = [f\"{n}. {b}\" for n, b in enumerate(body, 1)]\n    return PREAMBLE + \"\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(body)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":       # sanity tests of the verifiers\n    good = \"<<sea tips>>\\nahoy matey! i am captain byte.\\n* a remarkable tip\\n* another remarkable one\\n* last\\nany other questions?\"\n    for i in IDS:\n        assert check(i, good), i\n    bad = \"Hello, I am an assistant.\\n- one\\n\\nThanks.\"\n    assert not any(check(i, bad) for i in IDS if i != \"L_max\"), [i for i in IDS if check(i, bad)]\n    assert check(\"P_ahoy\", \"**<<Title>>**\\n\\nAhoy there\") and check(\"F_end\", \"Bye. **Any other questions?**\")\n    print(\"verifier tests ok\")\n------\n\"\"\"Score every generation against each (distinct) instruction in its system prompt.\n\nOutput: results/scores.csv, one row per (model, prompt, instruction) with compliance `ok` (0/1) plus design metadata.\n\"\"\"\nimport json, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport pandas as pd\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"src\"))\nfrom instructions import check, GROUP, INSTRUCTIONS\nfrom models import MODELS\n\n\ndef main():\n    prompts = {}\n    for fn in (\"prompts.jsonl\", \"prompts_numbered.jsonl\"):\n        prompts.update({p[\"pid\"]: p for p in map(json.loads, open(ROOT / \"data\" / fn))})\n    rows, summary = [], []\n    for key in MODELS:\n        f = ROOT / \"results/gens\" / f\"{key}.jsonl\"\n        if not f.exists():\n            continue\n        gens = {}\n        for l in open(f):\n            r = json.loads(l)\n            gens[r[\"pid\"]] = r                     # last write wins (resumed runs never duplicate, but be safe)\n        summary.append((key, len(gens), sum(g[\"finish\"] == \"length\" for g in gens.values())))\n        for pid, g in gens.items():\n            p = prompts[pid]\n            lines = [x for x in p[\"lines\"] if x != \"FILLER\"]\n            for iid in dict.fromkeys(lines):         # distinct, in order of first appearance\n                pos = p[\"lines\"].index(iid)          # 0-based slot of first occurrence (fillers count as slots)\n                rows.append(dict(model=key, pid=pid, exp=p[\"exp\"], cond=p[\"cond\"], task_id=p[\"task_id\"], k=p[\"k\"],\n                                 target=p.get(\"target\"), iid=iid, cat=INSTRUCTIONS[iid][\"cat\"], group=GROUP[iid],\n                                 pos=pos, n_lines=len(p[\"lines\"]), n_occ=p[\"lines\"].count(iid),\n                                 is_target=(iid == p.get(\"target\")), ok=int(check(iid, g[\"text\"])),\n                                 truncated=int(g[\"finish\"] == \"length\"), n_out=g[\"n_out\"],\n                                 others=\"|\".join(x for x in dict.fromkeys(lines) if x != iid)))\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    df.to_csv(ROOT / \"results/scores.csv\", index=False)\n    for s in summary:\n        print(\"%-14s gens=%5d truncated=%4d\" % s)\n    print(df.groupby([\"model\", \"exp\"]).ok.mean().unstack().round(3))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\nsrc/gen_server.py:1:\"\"\"Generate with the host's long-lived vLLM server (Qwen3-8B, OpenAI-compatible, :8011)