a judge \"safety reflex\" (refusals scored as compliance, 9/37 accuracy). Validate every logprob judgment (argmax==sampled token, mass>=0.5, retry, fall back to text). With validation, ~10–19 judgments/s.\n165:- Judge design that validated (37 hand labels): reply-only \"does the assistant decline?\" (34/37) + request+reply \"does the reply contain content that carries out the request?\" (35/37). cais/HarmBench-Mistral-7b-val-cls weights downloaded to the cache (~14 GB, 3 min).\n170:- No-dep server client: `/usr/bin/python3 -I` + urllib works against :8011 while the venv installs.\n172:- GPU0 was fully free 13:15–13:40; 7B/8B/14B AWQ all started first try with `kv_cache_memory_bytes` + gpu_memory_utilization=(budget+0.2)/48. :8011 Qwen3-8B did 3,150 short gens in ~25 min when idle, but crawled (~20/min) once other users loaded it to 110 concurrent requests.\n174:Update 2026-10-29 (context_window_cliff workspace, long-context 1K–32K probes, vLLM 0.32): no API key again; `uv add vllm` took ~15 min (slow copy, disk 98%). :8011 Qwen3-8B server was shared with another session (~30–45 running reqs) yet did 1,548 prompts of avg 12K tokens in ~110 min at 16 threads. All my local jobs auto-landed on GPU0 (100% util) → 7B-AWQ ~3.9 prompts/min at 16K avg; moving 1.5B/3B AWQ to the *idle* GPU1 4.2 GB slice cut ETA ~8× (actual use ≈ weights+kv+0.5 GB, so OVERHEAD=0.5, MARGIN=0.25 fits). Shuffling prompt order before running makes any partial run a uniform subsample — kill slow jobs at the deadline without losing design balance. Science gotcha: Phi-3-mini-4k (kaitchup GPTQ) has sliding_window 2047 honoured by vLLM → retrieval of facts >2K tokens from the question ≈0% (looks like a \"length cliff\").\n179:- The :8011 Qwen3-8B server was fast at first (~3.5k short chat requests in 90 s), then other users loaded it (48 running + 63 waiting), and the last ~2.5k 512-token code requests took ~2 h.\n183:Update 2026-10-30 (system_prompt_interference workspace, 7 models × 5.1k prompts, vLL