{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014LdxUr4KRjTMW2tETcF4yq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Curse of Instructions: Large Language Models Cannot Follow Multiple Instructions at Once\" Harada ManyIFEval\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.21051\"},{\"title\":\"alphaxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://alphaxiv.org/benchmarks/the-university-of-tokyo/manyifeval\"},{\"title\":\"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21051v1\"},{\"title\":\"the curse of instructions khi llm ngop tho vi qua nhieu yeu cau cung luc ymJXDDo6Jkq\",\"url\":\"https://viblo.asia/p/the-curse-of-instructions-khi-llm-ngop-tho-vi-qua-nhieu-yeu-cau-cung-luc-ymJXDDo6Jkq\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.21051?context=cs\"},{\"title\":\"Masachika Taniguchi\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/people/masachika-taniguchi/\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.21051v1\"},{\"title\":\"論文の概要: When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following\",\"url\":\"https://fugumt.com/fugumt/paper_check/2509.21051v1\"},{\"title\":\"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following\",\"url\":\"https://preview.aclanthology.org/dashboard/2025.findings-emnlp.896\"},{\"title\":\"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following\",\"url\":\"https://preview.aclanthology.org/new-sigs/2025.findings-emnlp.896/\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the ManyIFEval benchmark, but under a different title than the one you gave.\n\n- **Title mismatch:** ManyIFEval comes from a paper titled \"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following,\" by Keno Harada and six co-authors. It was submitted to arXiv as 2509.21051 in September 2025 and appears in Findings of EMNLP 2025 (Keno Harada, Yudai Yamazaki, Masachika Taniguchi, Edison Marrese-Taylor, Takeshi Kojima, Yusuke Iwasawa, Yutaka Matsuo).\n- **\"Curse of Instructions\" paper:** I found no primary source for this exact title. A Vietnamese blog post describes it as an ICLR 2025 paper by Harada et al. and links to OpenReview (Tóm tắt nghiên cứu ICLR 2025 — Harada et al.). I could not verify that venue or the paper itself, so treat it as unconfirmed.\n- **What ManyIFEval measures:** It extends IFEval to prompts with up to ten instructions, and a prompt is only considered successful if every single instruction is met.\n- **Main finding:** Performance falls as instruction counts rise. The arXiv abstract reports that performance consistently degrades as the number of instructions increases across ten LLMs. One example from the benchmark notes that DeepSeek-V3 achieves 88.5% on MMLU but only 19% prompt-level accuracy with 10 instructions on ManyIFEval.\n- **Companion benchmark:** StyleMBPP covers code generation with up to six instructions (extended from MBPP (Austin et al., 2021)).\n- **Sample sizes:** The authors report that relatively modest sample sizes (500 for ManyIFEval and 300 for StyleMBPP) are sufficient for performance estimation.\n- **Data and code:** The authors state that ManyIFEval/StyleMBPP data and evaluation codes are available at https://github.com/kenoharada/Multiple-Instructions-Following.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d14609fb-cedd-473d-b4a3-21afe836ae86","uuid":"eecdc2aa-4066-468a-b282-dcaa318f8ad7","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:29:03.420Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"Curse of Instructions: Large Language Models Cannot Follow Multiple Instructions at Once\" Harada ManyIFEval","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019tpFnE6H6PKyCKetCV7urr","content":[{"title":"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.21051"},{"title":"alphaxiv.org","url":"https://alphaxiv.org/benchmarks/the-university-of-tokyo/manyifeval"},{"title":"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.21051v1"},{"title":"the curse of instructions khi llm ngop tho vi qua nhieu yeu cau cung luc ymJXDDo6Jkq","url":"https://viblo.asia/p/the-curse-of-instructions-khi-llm-ngop-tho-vi-qua-nhieu-yeu-cau-cung-luc-ymJXDDo6Jkq"},{"title":"arxiv.org","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.21051?context=cs"},{"title":"Masachika Taniguchi","url":"https://aclanthology.org/people/masachika-taniguchi/"},{"title":"arxiv.org","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.21051v1"},{"title":"論文の概要: When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following","url":"https://fugumt.com/fugumt/paper_check/2509.21051v1"},{"title":"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following","url":"https://preview.aclanthology.org/dashboard/2025.findings-emnlp.896"},{"title":"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following","url":"https://preview.aclanthology.org/new-sigs/2025.findings-emnlp.896/"}]},"The search turned up the ManyIFEval benchmark, but under a different title than the one you gave.\n\n- **Title mismatch:** ManyIFEval comes from a paper titled \"When Instructions Multiply: Measuring and Estimating LLM Capabilities of Multiple Instructions Following,\" by Keno Harada and six co-authors. It was submitted to arXiv as 2509.21051 in September 2025 and appears in Findings of EMNLP 2025 (Keno Harada, Yudai Yamazaki, Masachika Taniguchi, Edison Marrese-Taylor, Takeshi Kojima, Yusuke Iwasawa, Yutaka Matsuo).\n- **\"Curse of Instructions\" paper:** I found no primary source for this exact title. A Vietnamese blog post describes it as an ICLR 2025 paper by Harada et al. and links to OpenReview (Tóm tắt nghiên cứu ICLR 2025 — Harada et al.). I could not verify that venue or the paper itself, so treat it as unconfirmed.\n- **What ManyIFEval measures:** It extends IFEval to prompts with up to ten instructions, and a prompt is only considered successful if every single instruction is met.\n- **Main finding:** Performance falls as instruction counts rise. The arXiv abstract reports that performance consistently degrades as the number of instructions increases across ten LLMs. One example from the benchmark notes that DeepSeek-V3 achieves 88.5% on MMLU but only 19% prompt-level accuracy with 10 instructions on ManyIFEval.\n- **Companion benchmark:** StyleMBPP covers code generation with up to six instructions (extended from MBPP (Austin et al., 2021)).\n- **Sample sizes:** The authors report that relatively modest sample sizes (500 for ManyIFEval and 300 for StyleMBPP) are sufficient for performance estimation.\n- **Data and code:** The authors state that ManyIFEval/StyleMBPP data and evaluation codes are available at https://github.com/kenoharada/Multiple-Instructions-Following."],"durationSeconds":8.04124768999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014LdxUr4KRjTMW2tETcF4yq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
