:** the paper now states that the logit-scale size trend is not significant (p = .09). The report's \"at least as steeply\" reads more firmly than that.\n- **Multiple-testing correction:** E2's Holm correction runs across 32 group-level cells, not across models as the report says.\n- **Interference varies by model:** the −30 pp bullets → closing phrase effect ranges from −69 to 0 across models. The no-comma → closing phrase effect comes from only two Llama models. The report's averages hide both, so the paper states them.\n- **Added from the raw data:** a per-instruction table, a truncation sensitivity figure (at most 0.5 pp on the mean), and the P_matey → P_name pair.\n- **Dropped figure:** the H5 figure had overlapping axis labels, and its table has all the same data plus more.\n\n## Citations\n- **Harada et al.:** the report's \"Curse of Instructions\" title couldn't be confirmed from a primary source, so I cited the paper that does introduce ManyIFEval, \"When Instructions Multiply\" (Findings of EMNLP 2025).\n- **Lost in the Middle:** Crossref and arXiv confirm TACL 2024, and arXiv gives the authors, so those details are correct in the bibliography.\n- **IFEval and ComplexBench:** these are cited as arXiv preprints.\n- **Literature basis:** no literature review stage ran, and the paper says so.\n\n## Formatting\n- **Style file:** `[final]` alone leaves the NeurIPS footer's track name undefined, so I defined it as blank. This also means the paper doesn't claim to be a NeurIPS publication.\n- **Examples:** `paper_examples/` holds only a README, so the formatting follows the style guide alone.\n- **Author:** `.neurico/idea.yaml` doesn't exist, so the author is `NeuriCo` as you specified.\n\n## Decision for you\nShould the corrected numbers become the primary results? I kept the report's numbers so the paper stays traceable to it, as you required, but a final submission should probably use the corrected ones. That would mean replacing the numbers in `scores.csv`, regenerating the tables and updating `REPORT.md`; the changes are mechanical.\n\nSources:\n- [When Instructions Multiply (arXiv)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.21051)\n- [When Instructions Multiply (ACL Anthology)](https://preview.aclanthology.org/new-sigs/2025.findings-emnlp.896/)","ttft_ms":2226,"type":"result","duration_ms":492645,"uuid":"db2bd20d-181f-479f-b1cb-5c52761a69db","ttft_stream_ms":976,"time_to_request_ms":534,"first_content_frame_ms":976,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
